Licence-key functionality lives in the closed backend, not in this repository
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Every piece of licence/entitlement logic (instance identity,
activation/renewal, the Community domain-limit check, entitlement
computation, communication with the licence server) lives inside the closed
backend binary, distributed only as a container image.
**This repository contains none of it.** This repository is published
without an open-source or source-available licence on its own code — see
`LICENSE` — so there is no separate "licence key functionality" clause to
reason about for this repository's own terms; the restriction that matters
— forbidding attempts to disable, patch around, or reverse-engineer the
licence checks inside the distributed backend image — is a term of
`EULA.md` (the only document granting usage rights over the distributed
images), not of a code licence on this repository. See `EULA.md` and
`docs/LICENSING.md` for what that covers.

